suite 168_approve_notification_suite.sql   # 0135 the approval notification told the OWNER 「위탁 승인 — 결제 대기」 while the same function's comment two lines above says 「요금 없음, '결제' 없음 … 이 단계에서 움직이는 돈은 없다」. Found by a peer verifying a DIFFERENT claim of mine about the client. ⚠ More exposed than the client strings it matches: those are read by a HOST on an admin console; this is a push to the OWNER's lock screen and is the only sentence most owners will ever see about this step. N1 drives the REAL lifecycle (club_request_district → claim_host → create_session → runner_commit → checkin → delegate_dog → approve_dog) and asserts THE ROW THE RPC WROTE, not prosrc — a source grep cannot tell a shipping title from one in an unreachable branch. It checks both halves: no 결제/청구/환불 in the title, AND the 20분 deadline plus 자리 survive there, because the title is what the owner sees first · N2 the REJECTION arm survived a whole-function recreation — the branch N1 never reaches, i.e. exactly what a careless recreate drops silently · **G1 SCHEMA-WIDE**: no function documenting itself as money-free emits a notification title claiming money, allowlist EMPTY. This defect was found by someone looking at something else, so a per-function pin would not have caught it. — N1 · N2 · G1
suite 169_club_session_board_suite.sql    # 0136 club_session_board — the MEMBER board (spec v2 S2). Sean ruling #9: "always fine; it's like a public dashboard" — so this projection is designed as a POSTER and admits nothing we would not put on one. **P4≡P5 is the anti-enumeration pair**: a denied session and a NONEXISTENT one both return ZERO ROWS and are compared to EACH OTHER, because a raise on one of them makes this an oracle over session ids (today's operational board does NOT have this property — 0053:229-250 — and the contract records the divergence rather than harmonising to it) · P1/P2 the gate's two arms, and P2 ASSERTS the guest holds no club_members row so the shell arm is proven a real OR rather than passing by luck · P6 a pending row is visible while withdrawn is hidden **from its own owner** (0053:333's self-arm is a private courtesy on the operational board; a public dashboard does not publish who was turned down, and a self-arm would make the board's contents depend on the reader) · P7 a dogless NON-RUNNER guest is crew (ruling #6 — the spec's `role='runner_attending'` would have dropped every guest; the pin asserts the role IS owner_attending so it tests the ruling rather than passing by luck) · P8 committing promotes out of crew (0043:238-240) · P9 동반견 visible at all (today they are on NO board, 0053:330) with no runner · **P14 vs P15 are DIFFERENT propositions**: P14 reads the OUT-column list off pg_proc (a column that does not exist cannot leak — shape), P15 asserts no returned text contains a known phone or money-shaped value (a fare interpolated into the `state` label passes P14 and fails P15) · **P16 R3 four ways** — at `proposed`, runner_name is NULL to a third party and non-NULL to the owner, the proposed runner and the **backup host**, that last arm being the nullable-column fail-open shape 151 B5 measured on club_incident_settle_quote (0116:425) · P17 acceptance makes the pairing public — pairs are public, courtships are not · P18 the nu