suite 178_companion_run_record_suite.sql  # 0146 the 동반 (self-run) walk gets a RECORD — Sean 2026-08-26 「also yes the self runs are still part of the pack. so yes.」 Until 0143 a 동반 dog could never hold a `runs` row (every insert into runs needs a booking_id; 동반 has none), so 0038:137 — the only writer of a MEASURED participant_activities row — could never fire for it, and the host was the one person guaranteed to get no record of the walk they led. `session_record_companion_run` upserts the single participant_activities row for (session, caller). **C0 IS THE PRECONDITION AND IT IS ASSERTED, NOT ASSUMED**: session_checkin (0030:262) already wrote a checkin_only row, which is WHY this is an upsert — if that stops being true, C1 silently becomes an insert test and C7's 「count stays 1」 measures nothing (0134's D4 lesson) · **C1 THE FK TRAP**: person_id must be the caller's session_people.id and must NOT be their profile id — 0131 shipped a draft arm reading `person_id = auth.uid()` that could never match and read as an own-row guarantee, and a non-null check passes on either; C1 also pins the row IDENTITY (same id before/after = a real UPSERT, not delete+insert) and the DERIVED pace (1800/4.2 → 429; a pace that is not derived is a fake number) · C2 flat battery = checkin_only with km AND pace null but the DURATION kept — Sean: 「rather than never having happened」 · C3 a seated participant WITH A LIVE 동반 DOG who never stamped in gets not_checked_in and writes ZERO rows — the dog is the pin: the first fixture joined dogless and the mutation battery showed C3 then reddened on a TOKEN SWAP while the real damage never reproduced · C4 the dogless crew (ruling #6) get no_companion_dog · **C5 A DELEGATED OWNER IS REFUSED, and this is the load-bearing separation**: that walk is recorded by 0038:137 off its own runs row at settle, so accepting them here would write the same walk twice — once measured by the server, once self-reported by the person who did not take it · **C6 a MIXED owner's record names the COMPANION dog**: session_checkin picks a dog by owner_profile_id with NO custody filter (0030:260) and may legitimately name either, so `custody = 'owner_handled'` is the conjunct actually doing the work · C7 re-finishing replaces (count 1, same row id) · C8 stranger not_joined · unauthenticated not_signed_in · the anon ROLE cannot reach the body at all (EXECUTE, not the gate) · C9 km 0..100 and duration 0..86400 under one `invalid_measure` token, AND a refusal leaves the previously stored record byte-intact · C10 the host gets one too, through 0134 §C's door · G1 the new definer both ways (PUBLIC/anon cannot, authenticated/service_role can — a negative-only ACL pin is green on a function nobody can call) · **G2 SCHEMA-WIDE over every writer of participant_activities**, which is the complete set of doors because the table carries no write policy at all (0030:139); the source scan STRIPS COMMENT LINES before matching (0143 writes `insert into participant_activities` inside its own prose, and a comment quoting the code it replaced matches every grep that hunts for it), and the sweep ASSERTS IT CAN SEE ITSELF — a regex that matches nothing is a vacuous green, the most expensive kind. — C0~C10 · G1~G2
