suite 184_board_impl_acl_suite.sql        # 0153 내부 보드 함수는 클라이언트 롤이 부를 수 없다 — 0147:190 이 authenticated 에게 EXECUTE 를 줬고, 그 함수는 p_access 를 유도하지 않고 **호출자가 준 값을 믿는다**. 프로덕션에서 실행으로 증명: 무관한 authenticated 가 p_access='host' 를 위조해 남의 세션에서 ownerName·runnerName·프로필 id·chargeState·refundState·payoutState·openIncidentId 를 받아냈다 (host 1마리/2185B vs none 0마리/663B). 0147 자신의 VERIFY 가 못 잡은 이유는 grantee 를 `PUBLIC` 하나만 확인했기 때문 — B1/B2 는 클라이언트 롤을 **이름으로** 열거한다. **B3/B4 는 과잉 회수 통제이고 선택이 아니다**: service_role 을 뺏거나 바깥 RPC 를 막으면 B1/B2 는 완벽히 통과하면서 누출 대신 장애가 된다. 각 팔이 못 보는 실패를 적으면 두 목록이 다르므로 진짜 통제 한 쌍이다. **B5 는 부재를 시끄럽게 실패시킨다** — 함수가 사라지면 위 팔이 전부 공허하게 초록이 된다. ⚠ 전 팔 `is distinct from` — has_function_privilege 는 NULL 을 돌려줄 수 있고 plpgsql 은 NULL 에 IF 를 받지 않아 bare IF 는 정확히 필요한 경우에 침묵한다. — 0153-B1~0153-B5
suite 187_gps_trace_bounds_suite.sql      # 0156 트레이스는 미래로 갈 수 없고, 커버리지가 0 과 미측정을 가른다 — 러너가 좌표와 **시각**을 모두 제공하는데 수집은 단조성과 8 m/s 만 봤고 도출은 상한이 없어서, 몇 시간 뒤로 찍은 그럴듯한 트레이스가 5 km 예약에 99 km 를 얼려 원장에 들어갔다. **오늘 돈이 움직이고 플래그와 무관하다.** G1 미래 거부 · **G2 통제: 평범한 트레이스는 여전히 통과** (너무 조인 상한이 실제 업로드를 막는 실패는 G1 이 못 본다) · G3 탭 이후 점은 계산 제외, 꼬리 없는 같은 트레이스와의 EQUALITY 로 고정 · G4 큰 구멍은 NULL · **G5 통제, 가장 중요: 촘촘한 정지 상태는 여전히 0.00** — 0152/183 의 「측정된 0」 과 「미측정」 구분이고, 이 팔이 없으면 「km=0 이면 NULL」 이 G4 를 통과하며 그 구분을 파괴한다 · G6 주석 제거 후 소스 + NO-SOURCE 팔 · G7 ACL 양방향. ⚠ 300 초 커버리지 상한은 잠정값이며 Sean 의 판단 사항 (codex 의 미해결 질문). — 0156-G1~0156-G7 [pin prefixes corrected 2026-08-31: this suite's labels in the file are `0156-G*`; the line said `0159-G*`, which is the pack-map slice's namespace]
suite 185_phone_switch_suite.sql          # 0154 phone collection gets the ops switch card registration already had. Sean 2026-08-28: 「guest is a member and needs a phone number enter thing.」 0133 landed set_my_phone and DELIBERATELY wired no client collection point, because contract §8's ship gate — counsel's revised 개인정보처리방침 — is unmet; but `ops_flags` had a switch for card registration and NONE for phone, so whoever wired a signup field turned host-sees-everyone on in the same commit. 0154-G1 the gate is shut FOUR ways (NULL · missing row · future-dated · plus the past-dated positive control, without which a reader that always answered false would pass) — the NO-ROW arm is the load-bearing one, because with a row present a NULL column never reaches the coalesce (171 R7's measured lesson) · **0154-G2 THE REFUSAL, both halves**: a closed gate RAISES `phone_collection_closed` **and writes nothing**, and the TOKEN is asserted rather than 「it raised」, because answering `invalid_phone` would tell a person with a perfectly good number that their number is wrong · **0154-G3 IS G2's CONTROL and a real one** — same user, same input, same statement, differing only in the flag; without it a `set_my_phone` broken outright would pass G2 perfectly · 0154-R1 `my_phone` returns MY number, NULL for someone with none, and carries **0 arguments** asserted against `pg_proc` (the absence of a target is a fact about the signature, and calling it can never prove it) · **0154-R2 NULL MEANS ONE THING** — 「no number」 is NULL while 「tombstoned」 and 「not signed in」 RAISE, so the settings screen cannot say 「번호를 등록해 주세요」 to a deleted account · **0154-W1 THE SLICE WIDENED NOTHING**: the column grants stay shut (this is NOT a duplicate of 127 W2 / 166 P6 — those pin the pre-existing refusal, this pins that 0154 left it intact while adding a reader), both new definers are anon-sealed, and three positive-control arms assert the doors that SHOULD be open are open · 0154-G4 the suite restored the flag, pinned rather than assumed because a failed restore poisons every later suite. ⚠ 166 gains a fixture arm + P8 for the same reason; every 166 proposition is unchanged. — 0154-G1~G4 · R1 · R2 · W1
suite 186_revocation_abandoned_alert_suite.sql  # 0155 카드 해지 포기는 보고된다 — Sean 2026-08-28 「the toss is fine, report to me」 (memo option ②). `abandoned` is reachable FOUR ways and only TWO are failures: the report at attempts>=8 and 0148's crashed-at-cap sweep ALERT; belt 2 (the key is somebody's current card) and 0148 §A's never-claimed revival are the system working correctly and stay SILENT — an alert that pages on healthy behaviour is muted within a week and then protects nothing. The classification is made AT THE SITE, never by matching `last_error` prose, so only moving an emitter call can break it. S1 the emitter's own shape (definer, in-body search_path, executable by nobody — 0155's VERIFY checks this at apply and a property checked only at apply survives exactly until someone recreates the function) · A1/A2/A3 and B1/B2 are two CONTROL PAIRS whose blind-spot lists differ: always-alert reddens A2+A3, never-alert reddens A1, and B1's fixture asserts its key is NOT in billing_keys because belt 2 runs first and would otherwise turn B1 into a weaker copy of B2 · B3 the revival, which is what makes 0155 not touching billing_key_swap a decision rather than an omission · C1 idempotence on the return value and the notification delta (`now()` is frozen in a do-block, so a timestamp comparison there could not fail and is not claimed) · C2 the `state = 'abandoned'` conjunct · **D1 the memo's actual finding** — `due_now` excluded `abandoned`, so the one dashboard-shaped object reported the queue clean PRECISELY BECAUSE rows were given up on · **D2 the non-widening pin**: due_now keeps 0150's sentence, with a genuinely-due arm so the column is not merely frozen · D3 both directions of `alert_recipients`, because `ops_recipients` is 0 rows in production and an alert to nobody must not read as an alert. — 0155-S1 ~ 0155-D3 (13 pins, incl. B4 the ordering)
suite 188_billing_hardening_suite.sql     # 0157 codex billing findings 5+6 — one key, ONE outstanding order to destroy it, and the cron is READ BACK. Two rows for one key mean two `DELETE /v1/billing/{key}` at Toss, and a successful first followed by a non-2xx second writes `abandoned` — which since 0155 PAGES a human to go hand-delete a key that is already gone, i.e. a duplicate turns a revocation that WORKED into the alert-fatigue 0155's own header warns about. All FIVE enqueue sites were enumerated before the index was written (a finding's SENTENCE is the property; the cited site is one place it is observable): billing_key_swap's three branches + `enqueue_billing_key_revocation` (delete-account) + the edge's `issued_unpersisted`. **0157-C1** the cron job read back from `cron.job` — active, schedule, command, AND the command's function EXISTS (a scheduler faithfully running `select no_such_fn()` is the same product outcome as no scheduler), with a LOUD absent-`cron.job` arm because otherwise every arm is vacuous. ⚠ C1 pins the job's SHAPE, not the swallow: `cron.schedule` upserts by name so 0138's identical registration survives deleting 0157 §A — the `exception when others` removal is proved two-sided by the APPLY (planted raising schedule: 0138's form applies GREEN, 0157's ABORTS), which no suite can observe. **0157-S1** the merge primitive's own shape (definer · in-body search_path · public/anon/authenticated refused · service_role kept as the positive control) — 0157's VERIFY checks it at apply and a property checked only at apply survives exactly until someone recreates the function. **0157-U1** the partial unique index, three arms with DIFFERENT blind spots: a second OUTSTANDING row refused **on SQLSTATE 23505** (not merely 「it raised」), a second TERMINAL-state row ADMITTED (a full unique index passes the first arm perfectly and ships the wrong product — this is the only arm that tells them apart), a different key admitted. **0157-U2** the merge does not RESURRECT: the fixture is a row MID-FLIGHT (processing, attempts 3, live token and lease) and state/attempts/claim_token/lease_until are asserted UNCHANGED — a merge that reset them would look like a tidy-up and would hand a held row back to the claimer, re-creating the defect inside the fix. **0157-U3** the same property through the REAL path (`billing_key_swap`'s gate_closed branch, called twice), with BOTH refusals asserted so a fix that stopped the duplicate by breaking the swap cannot pass. **0157-U4** the delete-account site, the one a reviewer is least likely to look at, plus its no-card control. **0157-U5** an empty key is refused LOUDLY and writes nothing, with a real-key control so 「refuses everything」 cannot pass. **0157-U6** an FK violation costs the PROVENANCE, never the KEY — both halves asserted. **0157-R1** the suite restored the registration flag U3 shut. ⚠ NAMED GAP: §B's duplicate-collapse block is deliberately UNPINNED — it runs once at apply against duplicates that cannot exist in an empty fixture, so every arm would pass unconditionally and no mutation could redden it; 0157's VERIFY ④ guards it instead. ⚠ Finding 7 (constant-time cron-secret compare) has no SQL surface and is pinned in `functions/_test/`. — 0157-C1 · S1 · U1~U6 · R1 (9 pins)
suite 189_settled_distance_suite.sql  # 0158 정산된 돈은 그 돈을 매긴 거리로 표시된다, 그리고 못 재는 러닝은 0km가 아니다 — codex run-end #9 + #8, continuing 0152/183's job one level up. **0158-L1 THE HEADLINE**: `my_ledger_rows` returned `bookings.km` (what the booking was SOLD at) beside a net priced from `runs.actual_km`, so a 5km booking settled at 1.8km read 「초코 · 5km」 over the 1.8km money — and its fixture ASSERTS ITS OWN DISAGREEMENT ZONE (planned 5.0 vs measured 1.8), because 156 P2 and 165 P6 are green on a fixture where the two candidate columns AGREE and therefore say nothing about this. **0158-L3 / W2 / W3 / B1 are the positive controls and none is optional** — a rule that refused every zero would pass every refusal arm here and be the same defect with the opposite sign: a run MEASURED at 0.00km still reports 0.00, and a week with NO runs still reports a TRUE 0 (deleting the coalesce outright answers NULL there and prints 「—km」 at a runner who correctly ran nothing). W1/W2/W3 are three arms whose blind-spot lists differ (always-NULL reddens W2 · always-0 reddens W1 · NULL-whenever-the-sum-is-0 reddens W3 alone). **0158-B2 IS THE RANKING PIN**: `order by <expr> desc` is NULLS FIRST in postgres, so deleting the coalesce alone would have put the dog nobody measured at RANK 1 — the same class with the sign flipped. **0158-M1 is the reader the review did not name and it SPENDS**: the weekly miles cron (0014:70) ranks owners by `sum(actual_km) desc` with no coalesce at all, so an owner whose only completed run last week was unmeasured sorted ahead of everyone who ran and took 200 하이 포인트. 0158-B5 the ACLs that four DROP+CREATEs discarded, with `proacl IS NULL` checked POSITIVELY (aclexplode(NULL) is zero rows, so an exists-test is silent on exactly the born-PUBLIC state). ⚠ The boards take no argument and cut at `limit 10`, so B1~B4 run under a PARK of every `runs.ended_at` in both weekly windows; **0158-B6 pins the restore**. ⚠ 165's `b_reasg` fixture is amended IN THIS SLICE — its run carried NULL km and NULL reason, so once §A reads `actual_km` the disclosure pin 165-P2 would have gone vacuously green. — 0158-L1~L3 · W1~W4 · B1~B6 · M1 (14 pins)
suite 190_pack_map_channel_suite.sql  # 0159 팩 지도 — Sean 2026-08-28 「everyone should see everyone else on the map during a club run session with a little runner icon. total public」. `pack-<sessionId>` broadcast: READ is public (anon included), WRITE is a CHECKED-IN participant inside the window. The window is the only thing 0159 had to invent — a club session has NO running state (0030:62, verified against every later `alter table club_sessions`), so a channel keyed on status alone opens the moment somebody schedules a walk. Four conjuncts, three of them facts that already occurred: open/full · somebody checked in · the host has not tapped 러닝 종료 (bookings.run_ended_at on a CLUB booking has one writer, 0144:456, because end_run_tx raises club_out_of_scope at 0083:383) · and the check-in band (0030:251) purely as the answer to inaction. 0159-E2 is the only pin in the repo that can see the `pack channel read` POLICY — 0108's `party channel read` has no topic guard, so every authenticated arm is green with it dropped and only an anon boundary execution catches it. Control pairs named in the header: R1/R2 (always-open vs always-shut), P1/P2 (admits-everybody vs admits-nobody) — 0159-S1~S5 · R1~R3 · P1~P3 · E1~E3 · M1~M3 · W1~W3 · N1 (21 pins)
suite 191_pack_publish_suite.sql  # 0160 팩 발행은 RPC 다 — codex 가 0159 를 REJECT/11 로 돌려보낸 두 가지가 소켓 쓰기로는 고칠 수 없는 것이었다: realtime 인가는 **소켓당 캐시**되므로 조인 때 한 번 통과한 참가자는 세션 종료·러닝 종료 뒤에도 계속 발행했고(#2), 페이로드는 **클라이언트가 작성**하므로 체크인한 공격자가 남의 profileId·이름으로 더 최신 시각을 찍을 수 있었다(#4 — 0159 §2 가 스스로 그렇게 적어 두고 대응을 클라이언트에 맡겼다). 0160 은 둘 다 구조로 닫는다: `club_pack_publish(p_session, p_lat, p_lng, p_age_ms)` 가 매 호출 당사자(체크인 = 단어 AND 스탬프)와 창을 다시 결정하고, 페이로드를 서버가 auth.uid()/profiles 에서 만들며(시그니처에 신원 인자가 아예 없다 — 0160-A2 가 카탈로그로 잰다), `pack channel write` 는 사라져 소켓 INSERT 를 받아줄 정책이 하나도 없다(0160-B1 이 진짜 체크인한 참가자로 경계에서 재고, 같은 사용자가 같은 롤에서 RPC 로는 성공한다 — 이 짝이 없으면 「문이 닫혔다」가 「전부 죽었다」와 구별되지 않는다). 🔴 **0160-A3 의 발산 구역 픽스처**(attendance='checked_in' 인데 checked_in_at 이 NULL)가 이 파일에서 가장 값비싼 한 행이다 — 0159 의 창은 스탬프를, 쓰기 팔은 단어를 봤고 두 술어가 갈리는 곳은 이 행뿐이라 양쪽이 일치하는 픽스처로는 규칙 변경을 볼 수 없다. 발행은 `realtime.send`(모든 오류를 삼킨다 — 운영 prosrc 측정 2026-08-31)가 아니라 **직접 INSERT** 이고, 실패는 자체 exception 블록이 `raise warning` + 유형화된 `not_delivered` 거절로 바꾼다 — 0160-S1 이 주석 제거 후 소스로 INSERT 와 그 변환의 존재를 재고, 0160-A1 은 행의 id 열 = payload id 까지 잰다(send 경로에서는 거짓이 되는 팔). serverNow(뷰어 시계 보정)·조회수 카운터(Sean 2026-08-31 「Yes, add counter」)·p_age_ms 과거-전용 클램프 포함. ⚠ 심의 realtime.messages 는 파티션이 없어 `not_delivered` 는 하네스에서 도달 불가, 스로틀 동시성도 단일 트랜잭션이라 도달 불가 — 둘 다 핀이 아니라 파일 머리의 산문이다(팔이 실패할 수 없는 핀은 산문의 일을 하는 위조 보증이다) — 0160-A1~A9 · B1 · S1 · W1~W3 · M1 · M2 (16핀)
suite 192_billing_keys_grants_suite.sql  # 0161 billing_keys 는 벽이 둘이다 — 0080:110 이후 RLS on + 정책 0개라 오늘 새는 곳은 없지만, Supabase 기본 권한이 준 anon/authenticated 의 테이블 권한이 회수된 적이 없었다(같은 자격증명을 나가는 길에 담는 자매 테이블 billing_key_revocations 는 0138:49 에서 첫날 회수했다). 「정책이 0개라서 안전하다」는 미래 슬라이스가 정책 하나를 더하는 순간 코드 변경 없이 무장한다. 0161-N1 여덟 팔(2롤 × 4권한) 부재 · **0161-N2 과잉 회수 통제**(service_role 의 SELECT/INSERT/UPDATE 와 my_billing_card 의 ACL — 전부 회수하면 N1 은 완벽히 통과하면서 카드 등록·해지가 조용히 죽는다) · **0161-N3 픽스처 통제**(같은 스키마의 평범한 테이블은 여전히 기본 권한을 갖고 있다 — 결함을 담지 않은 픽스처는 수정을 시험할 수 없다는 0151 의 기록) — 0161-N1~N3
