suite 196_revocation_findings_suite.sql  # 0166 codex's four SQL findings on 0155, each re-measured against trunk before building: F0 the new sweep helper's own envelope (definer · in-body search_path · nobody executes) · F1 the CRON tick reaches a row stranded at the attempt cap — 186's B1 calls the claimer directly and therefore assumes the worker it was invoked, which is exactly what the finding denies · F2 an empty ops roster no longer records itself as alerted, so provisioning a recipient later actually delivers (two arms: the false stamp, and the retry) · F3 a terminal row cannot be rewritten by a late token-less report — `p_token is null and claim_token is null` was true of every terminal row, and the crashed-at-cap row is where a late report is the EXPECTED event · F4 an abandon nobody classified is counted as `abandoned_unclassified`, never as benign (absence fails CLOSED). Findings 5/6 are repairs inside 186 rather than pins here. — F0~F4 (5 pins)
suite 197_phone_visibility_gate_suite.sql  # 0167 the collection switch gates VISIBILITY, not only writes — codex 0154 #3 (CRITICAL). 0154 gated the WRITE path (`set_my_phone`) and nothing else, so a number that arrived by any OTHER route (service_role, a backfill, a restore — and every phone fixture in this harness) was returnable while Sean's switch was still off. 0167 makes both read doors consult `phone_collection_live()`. **0167-P1 THE HEADLINE** — with the switch at its SHIPPED value a host↔member pair answers **false, not NULL** (`is distinct from false`, because a NULL-returning helper looks correct to every `if phone_ok then` while `case when phone_ok then phone end` is the only thing between the number and the payload), plus the propagation arms through `club_session_roster` (number gone from the payload AND no `club_phone_access_log` row) and the restore-by-VALUE arm · **0167-P2 / 0167-P4 ARE THE POSITIVE CONTROLS AND NEITHER IS OPTIONAL** — a helper hard-wired to false, or an `incident_contact` that nulled the column unconditionally, passes P1/P3 perfectly and ships a dead feature; the blind-spot lists differ by construction (refuse-everything reddens P2/P4 only, disclose-everything reddens P1/P3 only) · **0167-P3 THE SHAPE DOES NOT MOVE** — closed means `phone` NULL while `role`, `name` and the ROW COUNT stay, and nothing raises: zero rows already means 「not a party」 and 「no open incident」 (0088 §E, decoded as such at `api.ts:3559`), so the lazy fix would tell a person mid-incident there is no incident · 0167-P5 source, comments STRIPPED (0167's own header names the gate in prose), gate BEFORE the first select, with a NO-SOURCE arm. ⚠ `club_session_roster` is deliberately NOT edited (0165 owns it) — gating inside the helper propagates to both its call sites. ⚠ 67 H5 and 124 G7 arm the switch in their own fixtures in this slice; every proposition there is unchanged. — 0167-P1~P5 (5 pins)
suite 198_two_phase_stop_suite.sql  # 0168 두 단계 정지 — 호스트의 탭은 시계를 멈추고, 스윕이 돈을 얼린다. codex GPS finding 4, the one 0156's own header says it does NOT close. 러너의 폰은 60초 배치로만 업로드하므로 호스트가 탭하는 순간 최대 한 주기분의 **진짜 GPS**가 아직 서버에 없고, 부킹은 active 이므로 그 꼬리는 가격이 확정된 뒤에 도착해 아무도 지불하지 않는다. **오늘 돈이 움직이고 플래그와 무관하다** (러너의 ledger_items 는 payments_live_since 와 무관, 0083:754). **0168-P1 배수 창 안에 도착한 GPS는 돈이 된다** — 같은 기준 트레이스를 가진 쌍둥이와의 델타로(2.40 vs 2.00), 순수 거절이 왜 결함의 방향을 영구화하는지가 이 핀의 내용이다 · **0168-P2/P3 는 통제 한 쌍이고 이 파일이 존재하는 이유** — 닫힌 창은 run_stopping 으로 **이름을 붙여** 거절하고(토큰으로 잰다: 「예외가 났다」는 retryable 한 impossible_speed 와 구별되지 않는다), 열린 창은 여전히 받아들이며 받아들인 것은 거리가 된다. 못 보는 실패 목록이 서로 달라(과잉 거절 vs 과잉 수용) 「전부 거절」 수정이 P2 를 완벽히 통과하면서 P3 만 빨갛게 만든다. P2 는 **동결되지 않은** 세 번째 세션에서 재어, 거절의 원인이 배수 창임을 확정한다(동결된 절반은 176 P9 가 뒤집혀 소유한다) · **0168-P4 INACTION** — 탭하고 폰이 다시 말하지 않을 때: 스윕 전엔 스탬프도 km 도 없고 원장 0행, 스윕 후엔 도착한 것으로 도출되고 **탭 시각**으로 동결되며 원장은 여전히 0행. 크론은 cron.job 의 행으로 다시 읽고 그 명령이 부르는 함수의 존재까지 본다 · **0168-P5 0156 은 넓어지지 않았다** — 컷오프는 탭이지 스윕의 now() 가 아니다. 픽스처는 두 규칙이 **갈리는 구간에만** 점을 둔다(2.70 vs 옛 규칙 2.90) · 0168-P6 멱등성을 **핀이 스스로 일으킨 델타**로 (픽스처에서 물려받은 개수가 아니라 phase 2 를 한 번 더 돌린다) · **0168-P7 run_ended_at 은 뜻을 지킨다** — 1단계가 찍으면 settle-run 이 Number(null)===0 으로 0km 정산을 만들고(handler.ts:90,264-280) 0159 의 팩 지도가 러닝 도중 닫힌다; 창의 열림→닫힘을 델타로 잰다 · **0168-P8 가드가 읽는 것** — 행 락·컷오프·동결 시계, 주석 제거 후 소스로. 단일 연결 하네스에서 for update 는 행동으로 관측할 수단이 아예 없어 소스가 유일한 계기다. ⚠ 배수 창 90초·스윕 1분·도출 실패 시 stopping 유지는 전부 **잠정값이고 Sean 의 판단 사항**(계약 §8). ⚠ 176 은 같은 슬라이스에서 개정됐다(P9 뒤집힘, P1/P3/P4/P5/P11/P13 이동) — 0168-P1~P8 (8 pins)
suite 199_settle_stopping_belt_suite.sql  # 0169 the SQL belt behind 0168's 409 — `settle_run_tx` refuses a booking that is still `stopping` (run_stopping_at✓ · run_ended_at∅, the same predicate `settle-run/handler.ts:94` reads), closing the NAMED GAP 0168 wrote into its own header: the handler is the only door a CLIENT can reach (0083:838 revokes authenticated), but a `service_role` caller settles at the CLIENT's numbers with nothing in its way — 0168's own defect through a different door. **0169-B1** the attack verbatim (9.90 km handed in while the server has derived nothing) refused by name, with the ledger measured as a count BEFORE and AFTER and the booking's state unmoved (the refusal sits in front of the atomic claim) · **0169-B2 IS THE PIN THAT MAKES B1 WORTH HAVING** — the freeze does NOT clear `run_stopping_at` (0168:589-600), so a belt written as `run_stopping_at is not null` alone passes B1 perfectly and refuses **every club settle for ever**; after the shipped sweep (called with no arguments exactly as cron does) the same call settles on the server's 2.00 km, and its ⓐ arm shows 0083 ⓔ standing where the belt lifted (the client's 9.90 is still refused, now as `frozen_measurement_mismatch`) · **0169-B3** a run that was never stopped settles at the same moment B1 is refused — the fixture where the two candidate predicates diverge, and the marketplace never writes the stamp at all · **0169-B4** source, comments STRIPPED (0169 explains `run_stopping` inside the function's own comments, so an un-stripped check is satisfied by the explanation), asserting the refusal is positioned BEFORE the first UPDATE/INSERT — behaviour cannot see order, and 「refused before the claim」 vs 「wrote three rows and rolled back」 are the same ledger count. — 0169-B1~B4 (4 pins)
suite 200_billing_intent_suite.sql  # 0170 an issuance is NAMED before Toss is called — Toss provider memo §4's branch-independent core, closing the LOCAL half of codex billing findings 3/4. One durable intent row per issuance ATTEMPT, written BEFORE the provider call and carrying the server-minted Idempotency-Key that call is sent under; before 0170 that key was a `crypto.randomUUID()` minted inside the isolate and persisted nowhere, so a lost response left a live charging credential named in no table at all. 0170-B1 shape of both definers · B2 the two-wall seal (8 ACL arms + fixture control + over-revoke control) · B3 one intent per attempt and a retried open returns the SAME key (+ the constraint itself, 23505) · B4 a closed intent never reopens, through neither RPC · B5 two attempts can never share a key (Toss's dedupe tuple omits the BODY, memo §2a claim 8) and 300 chars is the ceiling (claim 11) · B6 party gate BEFORE state gate, neither refusal mints a key (+ positive control) · B7 the close is faithful and a contradictory outcome raises · B8 the registration flag is restored by VALUE (8 pins)
suite 201_phone_visible_null_safe_suite.sql  # 0171 codex deploy-gate #6 — an UNKNOWN custody phase is not a RESOLVED one. `_club_phone_visible`'s lifetime arm tested `custody_phase <> 'resolved'`, so an unrecorded phase fell out of the arm exactly as a finished custody does and, after session closure, the helper refused a live delegation. ⚠ READ 201's HEADER BEFORE READING ITS GREENS: the column is NOT NULL today (0040:47, measured) and a BEFORE trigger derives it, so P1's NULL is MANUFACTURED — it disables `club_v1_axes_sync` and drops the constraint, and P4 asserts both back by value. The pin is falsifiable (reverting the predicate reddens P1 alone, measured) but the STATE is not reachable in production; the finding's «nullable» came from the CLIENT projection contract (api.ts:4210), not from the column. **P1** NULL phase + flag ON + session `done` + host↔보호자 ⇒ visible, with three fixture-precondition arms so the green is attributable (session is `done` so the first lifetime branch cannot be doing the work; the REAL phase already answers true; `service_state` is not `ended`) · **P2 THE CONTROL** phase `resolved` ⇒ NOT visible — deleting the conjunct passes P1 and reddens only this · **P3** 0167's flag gate untouched: switch at its shipped value ⇒ false, not NULL, plus the flag restore asserted BY VALUE · **P4** the deployed source, comments STRIPPED (0171's own header quotes the bare operator in prose, so an unstripped check passes most surely on the best-documented bug), with a NO-SOURCE arm, plus this file's two schema guards asserted back up (`attnotnull`, `tgenabled` — the STATE, not `pg_get_triggerdef`)
suite 202_settle_charge_reconcile_suite.sql  # 0172 the settle-charge RECOVERY CHAIN is scheduled. ⚠ READ 202's HEADER BEFORE READING ITS GREENS: codex deploy-gate HIGH #1's premise is FALSE — the sweep it asked for already exists (`sweep_settled_without_payments`, 0080 §G / 0116 §A) and was MEASURED recovering the `CHARGE LOST` state end-to-end through end_run_tx → confirm_return_tx ×2 → the sweep (pending / 18,900 / basis_km 3.00, second sweep adds nothing). The recovery BEHAVIOUR is therefore pinned elsewhere and deliberately not re-pinned here (116 C9/C22/C24, 119 R10, 151 B1). What nothing asserted before 0172 is that either job of the chain is actually REGISTERED: both went in under the swallowing `exception when others` form 0157 §A condemned (0080:643, 0080:1259), so a failed install committed as a successful migration. **0172-S1** active `sweep-settled-charges` running `select sweep_settled_without_payments()`, exactly 1, with a NO-CRON-REGISTRY arm and a name-only-match diagnostic · **0172-S2** the same for `dispatch-due-charges` (a minted row nothing dispatches is the same revenue outcome as no row) · **0172-S3 THE CONTROL, and without it S1/S2 cannot fail** — the row is installed by 0080 on every apply, so the detector is proven able to report ABSENT: delete ⇒ 0, present-but-`active=false` ⇒ 0 (a name-only detector fails here), restored BY VALUE ⇒ 1 and byte-identical to the snapshot. ⚠ 0172's VERIFY and these pins are DIFFERENT ARTIFACTS and neither is evidence for the other — the shim always succeeds, so the harness structurally cannot reach the apply-time absence the VERIFY owns
suite 203_settled_without_payment_arm_suite.sql  # 0173 payments_reconciliation's EIGHTH arm, settled_without_payment — the only arm that can see a booking with NO payments row at all. sweep_settled_without_payments() SKIPS a settled run it cannot price (end_reason NULL 0116:100 / actual_km NULL 0116:112 / a mint that raised 0116:125) with nothing but a RAISE NOTICE, so before 0173 that booking was invisible to every ops query (fix-wave re-attack MEDIUM R2; 0172:88-94 named it as its own out-of-scope residual). Bookings-anchored on runs.settled_at — NEVER bookings.status, NEVER ledger_items presence (0116:47-52 refuses both by name and A4 is the control for each). **0173-A1** the arm sees it and names the SWEEP'S OWN reason in the sweep's own order (missing_end_reason / missing_actual_km / unpriced), with payment_id and amount empty because there is no payments row and a priced amount would be a number nobody computed · **0173-A2 THE CONTROL** a qualifying payments row makes the same booking disappear, kind-less widget debris does NOT (0116:96-106's deliberately-wider predicate, 151 B1 ⓒ′), deleting the row brings it back · **0173-A3** scope: inside the 1-hour grace the sweep still owns it (0118:1378's constant reused — the sweep has NO grace constant of its own, only a 5-minute cron cadence, so an hour is twelve failed sweeps), and payments_live_since NULL ⇒ the whole arm is 0 rows · **0173-A4** the anchor, both wrong substitutes in the flesh · **0173-A5** deployed source, comments STRIPPED, with a NO-SOURCE arm plus definer/search_path/ACL by value. ⚠ 0118:1372-1376 addressed a warning to whoever added arm eight — it emits NULL payment_id, as arm seven does, and 116 C11 / 120 J4 group by payment_id — measured: no shipped pin moved, because arm seven needs a CANCELLED club booking and arm eight needs a stamped settled run
suite 204_reconciliation_group_key_suite.sql  # 0174 payments_reconciliation() gets ROW_KEY, a per-row subject identity that is never NULL. 0118:1372-1376 warned that 116 C11 / 120 J4 assert disjointness with `group by payment_id having count(*) > 1` and SQL groups every NULL into ONE group; 0173 added the second NULL-emitting arm, and the wave-2 re-attack found the narrower case — two rows from arm EIGHT ALONE, on two different bookings, already collide, so the duplicate detector fires on a CORRECT board. row_key is `payment_id::text` on arms one…six (grouping byte-identical to before) and `booking:<booking_id>` on arms seven and eight, which exist precisely because there is no payments row. ⚠ Deliberately NOT prefixed with the arm name: that form gives a row claimed by two arms two distinct keys and DELETES the duplicate detection C11/J4 exist for — K3 is the pin that refuses it. **0174-K1** two NULL-payment_id rows from DIFFERENT arms, with the OLD key re-run on the same live query and required to COLLIDE, so the pin is a delta it caused rather than a state it found · **0174-K2** two rows from the SAME arm on two bookings (an arm-name key dies here) · **0174-K3** the control: board-wide, every payment-bearing row has row_key = payment_id::text — with the NAMED GAP that a one-row-two-arms fixture is unreachable (the arms are mutually exclusive on payments.status), so that half is measured by mutation (iii) instead of pinned · **0174-K4** no NULL and no empty-string key on a board proven non-empty and holding both NULL-payment arms — the non-vacuous version of 0174's own apply-time VERIFY. ⚠ 0174 DROPs and recreates the function: `create or replace` cannot widen a `returns table` (measured — `cannot change return type of existing function`), the ACL is restated verbatim in-file, and drop+create ride one transaction. — 0174-K1 ~ 0174-K4 (4 pins)
suite 207_open_drop_tx_suite.sql  # 0176 open_drop_tx — backend honesty audit H2/M3: the edge consumed a drop (CAS on opened_at) BEFORE paying it, so one failed writer burned the drop for good under 0106 §3; now ONE definer transaction, party gate → choice check → state gate → CAS → every reward, any raise rolls the CAS back. **0176-O1** party before state (an outsider on an OPENED drop gets not_drop_owner, never already_opened; no subject → not_signed_in; missing/NULL id → drop_not_found) · **0176-O2** the choice is judged before consumption — whitelist-outside / none / not-among-this-drop's-options / a choice on a mini all refuse bad_pick_choice with opened_at still NULL, then the same pick opens (24h boost row, applied {boost_until} only) · **0176-O3** mini pays miles 600 (drop) + card drop-15 레어 + gear claim in one call, applied exactly those three, second tap already_opened with rows unchanged · **0176-O4** pick miles → 5,000 (pick_drop) / gear → claim, pick_choice stored · **0176-O5 THE H2 PIN** a planted failing gear writer (trigger, owner-created, executed not source-planted) rolls the CAS back: opened_at NULL, miles 0 rows (the earlier insert undone), gear 0, the raise is the planted one (control), and the same drop then opens fully · **0176-O6** deployed shape by value: definer, in-body search_path, ACL (PUBLIC/anon/service_role ✗, authenticated ✓, proacl not default), comment-stripped source order (party + choice before the CAS), no swallowing handler · **0176-O7** a drop that would pay NOTHING (a mini {miles:0}, admitted by 0106's CHECK, minted by nobody) is refused drop_pays_nothing and stays unopened — H2 by INACTION. ⚠ 141 D19 (client-callable function touching drops = 0) now carries a one-entry allowlist for this function with a liveness arm — read D19's comment. — 0176-O1 ~ 0176-O7 (7 pins)
suite 208_cron_readback_suite.sql  # 0177 H3 + M10 — the four money/ops crons that were registered under `exception when others then raise notice` (club-payout-release 0045:443, run-end-recovery 0083:1512, cancel-money-gaps 0117:1652, sweep-club-cancel-fees 0118:1338) are re-registered STRICTLY and read back from `cron.job`; S1..S4 are one pin per job (four rows, so the count of reddened pins is the count of broken jobs) on (jobname, active, schedule, command), S5 is the control that manufactures four kinds of absence per job — gone / parked inactive / same name different command / same command re-staggered — and restores by value. ⚠ 0175's VERIFY and these pins prove DIFFERENT things: the VERIFY aborts a production apply, these redden when a LATER file unschedules or re-registers, and the harness structurally cannot reproduce the production cause (the shim's cron.schedule cannot fail). S6/S7 are M10: owner_la_sweep_stale takes pg_try_advisory_lock ahead of its first loop and releases on both exits (comment-stripped source pin with a raw>stripped arm proving the strip is load-bearing, plus a NO-SOURCE arm), and the definer/search_path/ACL envelope that makes those arms mean anything. A single-connection harness cannot exercise a session-scoped re-entrant lock, so the SHAPE is what is pinned and the header says so
suite 209_report_refusal_suite.sql  # 0178 report_billing_key_revocation NAMES its refusal — backend honesty audit M7, the server-side ④ instance: 0155's boolean meant 「lost the lease」 (0141 §C), 0166's `and state='processing'` gave `false` a second cause (a terminal or unclaimed row) and a third (no row), and revoke-billing-keys kept counting every false as stale. Now `(applied boolean, refusal text)` with absent · not_processing · lease_lost in that precedence, the UPDATE 0166's statement for statement. **0178-R1** a held row + wrong token ⇒ lease_lost, row untouched (also the token-less old call shape) · **0178-R2 THE DISAGREEMENT ZONE** a row nobody holds (done/abandoned/pending/failed) + null token ⇒ not_processing — the call 0155 APPLIED and 0166 refused indistinguishably from R1 — row byte-unchanged · **0178-R3** no such id / NULL ⇒ absent, exactly one row per call, nothing written · **0178-R4** precedence: done + wrong token ⇒ not_processing (not lease_lost), and the two sides of the line answer differently · **0178-R5** the control: a landed report is (true, NULL) on done/pending/abandoned, rows as 0166 left them, the second tap not_processing · **0178-R6** deployed shape (TABLE(applied, refusal), one overload, definer, search_path, ACL service_role-only, comment-stripped source carries 0166's conjunct + three tokens, no swallowing handler) + the LEDGER: no observed pair is (false,NULL) or (true,token). ⚠ 174 L3 / 186 A1–A3 / 196 F2–F3 read the boolean by value and now read `applied` (suite-update law, reason at each site). — 0178-R1 ~ 0178-R6 (6 pins)
suite 210_booking_hold_idempotency_suite.sql  # 0179 the booking hold is ONE transaction with an idempotency key — backend honesty audit §(a) #3: create-booking-hold had no key, a double-submit made two bookings, and its four writes + CAS were not a transaction. `bookings.client_request_id` + a PARTIAL unique index on (owner_id, client_request_id) (0162's chat shape) and `create_booking_hold_tx` (service_role-only, the settle_run_tx shape): party gate BEFORE any read → key lock then dog lock (fixed order) → replay (same owner+key ⇒ the same row, unchanged:true; a reused key with a different slot/money payload ⇒ request_mismatch) → the clash guard, atomic with the insert → the ladder, the hold, the CAS. NULL key = no idempotency (installed builds). **0179-K1** replay returns the same id, +1 row, +1 hold, and tells the truth about what the row has become · **K2** mismatch on km/time/dog refuses and writes nothing; the analytics snapshot is not compared · **K3** two keys ⇒ two rows; NULL keys ⇒ the pre-slice contract · **K4** the overlap guard is key-independent and per dog; a stale payment_hold does not block · **K5** party before any read — stranger's/absent dog, stranger's address, even with a replaying key ⇒ forbidden; NULL owner ⇒ not_signed_in · **K6 atomicity** a planted hold-insert failure rolls the booking back and the key is not consumed · **K7** close_to_matching=false ⇒ payment_hold; hold and booking rows carry exactly what was handed in · **K8** deployed shape + the belt exercised (a direct duplicate (owner,key) insert is 23505; NULL keys never collide) + source ORDER (party → locks key→dog → replay read; clash → insert; no exception handler). — 0179-K1 ~ 0179-K8 (8 pins)
