suite 237_ops_console_v2_suite.sql  # 0206 — 운영 콘솔의 없던 문 셋. **① 좌초 반환**: resolve_return(0193 §C-b + 0201 §C, 한국어 거절 맵 완비)은 트렁크 fde88a1에서 app/ 참조 0건이었다 — 팔 ⓕ의 종이 운영자를 psql로 불렀다. `ops_stranded_returns()`는 그 종 뒤의 목록이고 게이트는 return_strand(문이 쓰는 그 명부; payout_due로 잠그면 이름을 다 읽힌 뒤 not_ops가 나는 죽은 버튼). 술어는 팔 ⓕ(0201:737-742)의 것을 조항 그대로, 다른 점은 둘뿐 — 「이미 울린 종」 제외절이 **포함**으로 뒤집히고(종 시각은 notified_at), limit이 없다. **② 멈춘 인계**: `ops_stalled_handoffs()` — handoff_escalated_at/handoff_ops_alerted_at(0183)을 운영자 쪽에서 읽는 곳이 없었다. 게이트는 handoff_unanswered, 술어는 팔 ⓔ의 재확인, status는 부정 목록. 읽기뿐 — 멈춘 인계가 무엇이 되어야 하는지는 Sean의 결정이다(0183 팔 ⓓ 헤더). **③ 굿즈 종**: 0195는 스스로 「notifications untouched」였다 — `claim_gear_tx`를 0195 본문에서 재선언(0202는 이 함수를 건드리지 않았다, 측정)하고 payout_due 명부에 kind=system 「굿즈 수령 신청 — 확인 필요」 한 건을 ⑦ 쓰기 **뒤**에 넣는다(④ 조기 반환·모든 raise 아래 ⇒ 재탭도 거절도 종을 울리지 않는다). ACL은 이 파일에서 다시 적는다. **0206-R1** 읽기 전 게이트 — 여섯 형태가 not_ops이고 **좌초 없는 세계와 있는 세계에서 같은 낱말**(두 세계가 다르다는 대조 포함), 무기명은 not_signed_in, ops_me().kinds와 양방향 일치 · **R2** 목록 = **실제로 틱을 돌린 스윕이 종을 울린 집합**(복사본 대조가 아니다; 들어올 셋·빠질 넷을 이름으로) · **R3** 사실은 행의 것 — 양쪽 스탬프 + 미봉인 incident_review가 들어온다(0201 codex #2), to_jsonb 전체 훑기로 요금·전화·주소·계좌·메모 없음 · **H1** 두 명부는 서로 다르다(return_strand 운영자는 인계 목록에서, handoff_unanswered 운영자는 좌초 목록에서 거절) · **H2** 승격 뒤 나타나고 상대 확인 시 빠진다(형제 행은 남는다 = 빈 목록과 구별) · **G1** 종은 정확히 한 번, 거절엔 0건 · **S1** 배포 형상(제목·부정 목록을 **배포된 스윕**과 대조, 종은 멱등 반환/쓰기 단언 아래). ⚠ 이 스위트는 스윕을 실제로 5회 틱하므로 매니페스트의 **맨 끝**에 있어야 한다.
suite 234_availability_exceptions_suite.sql  # 0203 — 예외 일정(휴가·다구간). 0001:99가 `runner_availability_exceptions`를 만들었고 0002:78이 self 정책을 붙였고 **0003 §2는 그걸 줄곧 휴가로 읽어 왔다** — 없던 것은 WRITER다(`grep -rn runner_availability_exceptions app/` → 0행). 그래서 화면은 「예외 일정은 준비 중」이라고 적혀 있었고 서버에는 문 없는 기계가 있었다. 0203은 그 테이블에 kind(blackout|extra)·KST 날짜 범위·분 단위 창·created_at을 주고, 쓰기를 **RPC 둘로만** 좁히며(authenticated의 직접 INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE 회수 — 정책은 「누구의 행인가」는 말해도 「90일」·「하루 한 구간」·「최대 20건」은 말하지 못한다), 세 가용성 술어 중 **예약 경로가 쓰는 0003 `is_slot_available` 하나만** 넓힌다: §1은 그 날짜의 extra를 **OR**로 받고(주간 그리드는 그대로), §2는 blackout으로 **갈라서** 날짜 범위로 비교한다(kind 필터가 없으면 extra가 자기 자신을 막는다). 0015·0054는 손대지 않는다 — 0054는 수락 게이트의 거울이고(index.ts:174-176이 규칙을 안 읽는 이유를 적어 뒀다) 거기에 휴가를 넣으면 표시가 서버보다 엄격해져 공급이 조용히 증발한다. **0203-E1** 휴가 = 회수(전 true → 후 false, 같은 픽스처의 델타 · 지우면 돌아온다 · 파생 starts_at/ends_at이 KST 자정과 다음 날 자정) · **E2** 추가 근무 = 개방, **그 창만**(창 밖 시각·다른 날짜는 false로 남는다) · **E3** 휴가 > 추가 근무 — 같은 날 extra가 연 슬롯이 blackout으로 닫히고 blackout을 지우면 열린다(양쪽 대조로 false의 원인을 고정) · **E4** 남의 달력 — 0건 읽기(주인은 읽는다는 대조)·남의 id 삭제는 not_found이고 행은 산다·없는 uuid도 같은 한 단어(존재 오라클 아님)·🔴 쓰기 RPC의 **인자 목록에 러너가 없다**(게이트가 조건절이 아니라 부재라서, 이 팔이 없으면 p_runner가 생겨도 아무것도 안 빨개진다)·직접 쓰기 3종 42501·anon 42501에 authenticated 통과 대조 · **E5** 거절 낱말 전수(bad_kind·bad_range 둘·range_too_long과 90일 경계 대조·bad_window 네 방향·note_too_long과 40자 대조·not_runner·not_authenticated 둘·too_many 20/21과 「지난 행은 할당량을 안 쓴다」 대조) · **S1** 배포 형상(세 함수 definer·본문 search_path·ACL 양방향 + 엣지 service_role 대조 · 주석 벗긴 판정 본문에서 예외 테이블 **정확히 2회**·kind 필터 **정확히 2개**·daterange·주간 그리드 팔 생존·[0203] 주석으로 벗김 자체를 대조 · RLS·for-all 정책 제거·self-read만·쓰기 회수·anon 읽기 없음·새 칸 5·CHECK 4). ⚠ 명시된 갭: `not valid` CHECK 벨트가 거절하는 장면은 이 하네스가 도달할 수 없다(유일한 writer인 RPC가 낱말로 먼저 거절하고, 직접 INSERT는 회수됐다) — 존재만 S1이 재고 집행은 안 잰다. 산문으로 적고 핀으로 쓰지 않는다 — 0203-E1 ~ 0203-S1 (6 pins)
suite 238_owner_payment_state_suite.sql  # 0207 — the owner is told the payment STATE, not a row count. `0173` added arm eight to `payments_reconciliation()` (SETTLED booking, no qualifying payments row, past an hour of five-minute sweeps) and `0172 §A` reads the sweep's cron row back — but both are ops machinery: the function is `revoke execute … from authenticated` with NO runtime caller. The owner's screen reads the other side of the same fact and draws the opposite conclusion: `fetchBookingPayments` counts `payments` rows and `owner/schedule.tsx` renders 0 rows as 「아직 청구 내역이 없어요 — 정산이 끝나면 여기에 표시돼요」, which is true of a booking still settling and FALSE of exactly the population arm eight exists to report. A count is not a state, and 0 rows has two meanings. §A adds `my_booking_payment_state(p_booking)` — owner-only party gate BEFORE any read (a payment state is the PAYER's fact; the runner's money view is `ledger_items`), exactly one flat row always, and eleven states each derived from a deployed predicate and none invented: no_charge (the mint's cutover pair 0084:264-266) · awaiting_settlement (arm eight's anchor) · settling (inside arm eight's 1h grace) · settled_without_payment (arm eight itself, with arm eight's own reason case in its own order) · charge_pending · charge_retrying (charge_row_due ⓐ) · arrears (arm four, or the relink conjunct) · charged · waived · refunded · unknown (the fail-closed arm for a vocabulary widened later). THIS IS A READ — it mints nothing and changes no sweep. **0207-P1** the screen and the ops board agree as SETS over nine fixtures straddling every conjunct, board observed reporting first · **P2** the reason is the sweep's own refusal in the sweep's own order, read from BOTH surfaces, and the amount is never guessed · **P3** a payments row decides — all six statuses, with the relink conjunct observed independently of the attempt count · **P4** the cutover pair both directions, the unsettled run, and the grace boundary crossed on the clock alone · **P5** runner · stranger · non-existent booking all get one identical `not_party` (the only evidence of ORDER from outside), anonymous gets `not_authenticated`, owner passes · **P6** exactly one row always in both flag worlds, amount NULL exactly when no row answered · **P7** the wider qualifying predicate, measured in the divergence zone (kind-less debris does not answer; a kind-bearing canceled row does) · **S1** deployed shape + gate-before-read in comment-stripped source · **S2** every status the CHECK admits has an arm, literals read out of `pg_constraint` — 0207-P1…P7 · S1 · S2 (9 pins)
suite 239_ops_roster_suite.sql  # 0208 — `ops_recipients`(0084 §E)는 이 제품이 내보내는 모든 운영 알림의 수신자를 정하고 0198부터는 **콘솔에 들어올 수 있는 사람**까지 정하는데, 읽는 문도 쓰는 문도 없었다(trunk debe82e 측정: 픽스처 밖 insert/update 0건, app/ 참조 0건) — 운영자는 프로덕션에 SQL을 직접 쳐야만 생겼고 2026-09-22에 Sean이 자기 자신에게 바로 그렇게 했다. §B/§C/§D가 문 셋을 더한다: 전부 다른 다섯 ops 문과 **같은 창구**(ops_recipients_for('payout_due'))로 게이트하고, 게이트가 **인자보다 먼저**라 남에게는 존재하는 프로필과 없는 uuid가 같은 말을 듣는다. 0084 §E의 봉인은 뒤집지 않는다 — 정책 0·그랜트 0 그대로이고 더해지는 것은 definer 세 개뿐이며, **첫 운영자는 여전히 psql이다**(모든 문이 이미 있는 운영자를 요구하므로 구조적으로). §A는 봉인 장부 ops_roster_changes (누가·누구를·어느 클래스에·결과 상태, FK 없음 — 0186 §A·0194 §D). **0208-G1** 세 문 모두 게이트 우선·비신탁(존재/부재/없는 클래스/널이 모두 not_ops, 로그아웃은 not_signed_in, 운영자는 성공 — 대조) · **R1** 앉히기=행+장부 델타 1, 같은 값 재설정=changed false·델타 0, 내리기는 행을 **남기고** active=false (명부엔 보이고 라우팅 창구엔 안 보인다), 재개해도 created_at 불변 · **L1** 활성 payout_due가 하나뿐인 세계를 명시적으로 만들어(같은 표를 쓰는 열한 스위트를 저장·중립화·복원, 양쪽 대조) 마지막 하나는 본인도 못 끈다(last_operator, 행 불변, 장부 불변); 둘째를 앉히면 같은 내리기가 성공하고(대조) payout_due에만 건다 · **C1** 클래스 허용목록을 **집합**으로(방출자에서 뽑은 열세 이름 전부 수용, 오타·지어낸 이름·널·빈 값은 unknown_class이고 행도 장부도 안 남긴다) · **P1** 조회는 세 칸(pg_proc.proargnames로 — 값으로 보면 전화 없는 픽스처에서 늘 초록), 심어 둔 전화번호는 결과 어디에도 없고, 12명 중 10행, %·_는 리터럴, 탈퇴는 후보 아님, 한 글자는 short_query · **S1** 배포 형상(definer·본문 search_path·NULL-ACL 팔 먼저·ACL 양방향; 주석 벗긴 prosrc에서 게이트가 읽기보다 앞, 허용목록 열세 이름, for update, 장부 기록, delete 부재, on conflict의 created_at 부재, 조회의 phone/handle/district/avatar 부재; 장부 봉인·FK 0; 0084 §E 봉인 유지; NO-FUNCTION·NO-SOURCE·크루드 대조) — 0208-G1·R1·L1·C1·P1·S1 (6 pins)

suite 240_ledger_month_totals_suite.sql  # 0209 — the runner's earnings get a KST SHAPE. `my_ledger_rows` (0121 §A) carries `limit 30`, so a runner who has done more than thirty runs cannot see last month at all and one who has done fewer cannot either — thirty undated rows are not a month; between `my_ledger_unpaid_total` (0192 §B) and `my_ledger_total` (0027/0121 §F) there was nothing. §A `my_ledger_month_totals(p_months int default 6)` groups the SAME rows under the SAME summand by KST month, net only (Sean 2026-08-24 마진 비밀 — a month net is a sum of numbers already on the screen and admits no subtraction; a gross or fee column would undo in one line what that ruling removed from thirty rows), and `paid_won` is that same net split by 0186's marker rather than a second money axis. §B appends `dogs.neutered` — collected since 0001:44, written by owner/dog.tsx, read by ZERO runner-facing surfaces — to the two request views (0121 §D), `create or replace` and APPENDED, with 0121:150-153's four ACL lines restated. **0209-M1** the month boundary is Korea's: two rows ONE SECOND apart straddle a KST month start and land in different months while sharing a UTC month (the fixture asserts that collision, or the pin measures nothing), a row written at 23:59 UTC lands in the NEXT KST month, and the whole read is identical under America/New_York and Asia/Seoul — 0121's M3 dropped exactly this wrapping and came back GREEN because the harness machine ran KST · **M2** Σ of the month nets **equals** `my_ledger_total()` on the same fixture (the transcribed summand measured as a result, not promised), with the function's OWN row order read back as newest-first · **M3** a payment through the REAL ops door moves that month's `paid_won` 0 → exactly those rows' net as a before/after delta, `net_won` does not move, and `paid_won` stays STRICTLY below it because an unpaid comp row shares the month (a copy of net_won is visible only there); controls — the other two months stay 0 · **M4** the second runner gets their own single month whose net equals THEIR lifetime total (a leaked row breaks the equality even when the month count is right), an owner gets 0 rows and no raise, anonymous gets not_authenticated, and 🔴 the gate is an ABSENCE — no subject argument in proargnames (with p_months as the control that the count is not free), because a `p_runner` added later reddens no behavioural arm where caller and subject are one person (0203 E4) · **M5** the window is KST months back: 1 · 3 · 24 with the M-8 row as the control that the exclusions excluded something, the default measured BOTH by an explicit NULL and by an argument-less call, and 0/-5/9999 compared as whole result sets against their clamp targets (which differ from each other, so the comparisons are not vacuous) · **N1** both views carry `neutered` at its ACTUAL value in all THREE states — true, false, and NULL for an owner who never answered, which no constant satisfies — with 0121 §D's fare seal still shut and the anon/authenticated grants unchanged in both directions · **S1** deployed shape (definer · in-body search_path · ACL both ways, NULL arm first · no margin column and no subject in proargnames · comment-stripped source: both date_truncs on a KST WALL CLOCK, the row scope, the anonymous refusal, ledger_items read exactly once, and a TWO-SIDED crude control that the stripper ran · 0121:224's table seal intact · NO-FUNCTION/NO-SOURCE loud). — 0209-M1 ~ M5 · N1 · S1 (7 pins)
suite 241_ops_category_and_payout_stuck_suite.sql  # 0210 — ops alerts stop being filed as 안전·긴급, the unknown kind stops failing open into always-on, and the runner whose payout is stuck is told. 0189's `_noti_push_category` opened `p_kind in ('safety','system') then 'safety'` and `notify_push` RETURNS before reading `notification_prefs` for that category — so every ops escalation (지급 대기 0186/0190 · 인계 확인 멈춤 0183/0201 · 반환 좌초 0193/0201 · 굿즈 수령 신청 0206) was undisableable, and `notification-settings.tsx` explained that to the operator with 「개와 사람이 걸린 일이라서예요」 — true of an SOS, false of a goods-shipping desk ping. 0210 adds a fifth column `ops` (default true, opt-out), maps `system` → 'ops', and leaves `safety` plus `_noti_urgent_noti_titles()` exactly where they were (none of the four ops titles is in that array — measured, which is what makes the move safe). The `else 'safety'` fallthrough — the unknown-kind arm, reachable today by the writer-less `shop` member — moves to `booking`: still SENT by default (only an explicit false suppresses), no longer born un-silenceable. And `ops_payouts_stuck_sweep` (0186 §D → 0190 §A) told the ops roster and nobody else: the runner whose money it is, who may be the reason it is stuck (no `bank_accounts` row), now gets one `kind=booking` row per week — 「정산 지급이 늦어지고 있어요」, ref_id NULL → /runner/earnings via REFLESS_BOOKING_DESTINATIONS — whose body names THEIR amount and says 「정산 계좌를 확인해주세요」 only when the bank read says there is no account. **0210-O1** ops gates `system` and only ops does (control first, cross arms, the row survives) · **O2** all five off and safety/urgent still push while the four real ops titles go silent, plus the attribution arm that none of them is in the urgent array · **C1** the classifier's answer for every enum member BY VALUE incl. shop→booking and near-miss titles · **F1** the unknown kind pushes with no row, is silenced by `booking=false`, is not silenced by `ops=false` (a fixture in the zone where the old and new rules DISAGREE) · **R1** five columns through both RPCs and a 4-argument positional call leaves `ops` alone (the pre-0210 client's shape) · **P1** the real sweep tells the runner exactly once with their own unpaid total, the ops bell still rings, a 2-day-old runner gets nothing · **P2** the second tick adds nothing while the candidate still qualifies, and an aged notification lets the next one speak · **P3** two runners in ONE tick differing only in `bank_accounts` get different sentences · **S1** deployed shape incl. the 4-argument setter being GONE. — 0210-O1 ~ 0210-S1 (9 pins)
suite 243_chat_read_state_suite.sql  # 0212 — chat had NO read state at all: `chat_threads` is id/booking_id/created_at (0001:360-363) and nothing in the schema recorded who had read what, so neither an unread count nor a read receipt was computable — while `notification_prefs.chat` (0187 §A) already offered a 채팅 switch for a category the app could not show a count for anywhere, and every chat entry point (owner home hero · runner home job row · schedule sheet chip) was a button carrying no information at all. A count of this kind cannot be faked client-side either: the client holds the newest 100 messages of the ONE thread it has open and has never seen the others. 0212 adds `chat_reads (thread_id, profile_id, last_read_at)` — RLS self-read, no client write grant and no write policy — plus three definers: `chat_mark_read` (party gate on **is_booking_party**, the READ predicate, before any write; monotonic by construction via `greatest` in the on-conflict arm), `my_chat_unread()` (live set = **is_booking_party_active**, the same predicate that decides whether the caller could REPLY, never a re-derived status list; unread = the OTHER party's messages newer than the caller's own position, absent row read as -infinity; zero-unread threads ARE returned so 「absent」 and 「zero」 stay different answers) and `chat_thread_read_state(p_thread)` (the COUNTERPART's time and only theirs, one row always, NULL when never read or when the booking has no runner yet). **0212-M1** the position moves forward and never backwards — first call creates the row (0→1 delta), a planted PAST position advances, a planted FUTURE position survives, and all three report the STORED value rather than the one they tried to write · **U1** the count is the peer's newer messages in a fixture where peer=3 · all=5 · mine=2 are three different numbers, drops to 0 on mark-read while the RUNNER's number is unchanged in the same tick, and STAYS 0 when the caller sends two messages after their own read position (the one zone where including own messages reads 2) · **U2** one owner's three threads — confirmed+messages in, **cancelled_owner+messages out** (with its message count asserted first, so absence ≠ empty world; the zone where the two party predicates disagree), quiet confirmed in with 0/NULL; stranger sees none, anonymous is refused · **G1** stranger gets the identical not_party for a real thread and a random uuid on both thread-taking functions, anonymous gets not_authenticated from all three, the runner passes — and `chat_reads` is still 0 rows after every refusal (gate-before-write measured, not read) · **R1** both parties read one row of NULL before anyone reads; after the OWNER reads the runner sees that time and the owner still sees NULL; with both stored at DIFFERENT values each caller reads the OTHER's; a runner-less booking answers one NULL · **S1** deployed shape incl. `my_chat_unread` pronargs 0 and a two-sided control that the comment stripper ran. — 0212-M1 ~ 0212-S1 (6 pins)
suite 244_ledger_stuck_state_suite.sql  # 0213 — the runner's home strip stops reading a 30-row window and calling it 「all my money」. 0210 §E taught the SERVER to tell a runner their payout is stuck and `payout-status.ts`'s `payoutStuckDays` let the SCREEN say it too — off `fetchLedger()` → `my_ledger_rows()` (0121 §A → 0192 §A), which carries **`limit 30` ordered `created_at desc`**. But the answer is the OLDEST qualifying row, and a cap on a DESCENDING order keeps the thirty NEWEST and discards precisely the end the answer lives at: a runner past thirty rows got a SHORTER number or no strip at all, and those are exactly the runners 0210 §E exists for. Wrong in the flattering direction, for the busiest people, silently — and 0210 SAID SO in a 🔴 paragraph, which made the behaviour honest and left the screen wrong. §A `my_ledger_stuck_state()` returns ONE flat row over every row the runner owns, no limit: `unpaid_won` (0192 §B's predicate — unpaid, settled or not) beside `oldest_awaiting_at`/`awaiting_count` (the sweep's candidate predicate — unpaid AND 0186 §0d ⓒ's 「no run on this booking is still open」), because collapsing the two moduli because they are equal on most fixtures is what would put rows the writer refuses to pay into an age; plus `has_bank_account`, the same `exists` read 0210 §E does before choosing its sentence (a boolean — no bank, no holder, no ciphertext). Party gate is an ABSENCE: no subject argument, `auth.uid()` is the sole conjunct of both reads. **0213-A1** the answer comes from the row the cap hid — 35 settled unpaid rows aged 1…35 days, `oldest_awaiting_at` is row 35's own `created_at` read back from the ROW, with the control that the same caller's `my_ledger_rows()` returns exactly 30, its oldest is strictly NEWER, and row 35 is not in it at all (the fixture sits where the two reads DISAGREE — the 175-V2 law) · **A2** `unpaid_won` equals `my_ledger_unpaid_total()` as a RESULT, on a fixture whose unsettled unpaid row makes the two moduli genuinely different numbers (asserted FIRST, or a one-predicate implementation passes by luck) · **A3** one real `ops_payouts_stuck_sweep()` tick: the runner whose oldest SETTLED-unpaid row is 35 days old is told and the one whose is 3 days old is not — though both hold a 60-day unpaid row whose run is still open, and the second reads 3 days rather than 60 (reader and writer see one world) · **A4** one row, the caller's own; a profile with no ledger rows gets ONE row of measured zeros and a NULL instant, never zero rows; anonymous is refused by name · **A5** `has_bank_account` is attributable to the row — two runners in the same instant differ only in it, then insert/delete moves it both ways · **S1** deployed shape: definer + in-body search_path, ACL both directions, no subject argument in proargnames, no margin or bank field in the OUT list, and the comment-stripped body with no `limit`, both reads scoped to `auth.uid()`, the settled conjunct present, a NO-SOURCE arm and a TWO-SIDED stripper control. — 0213-A1 ~ A5 · S1 (6 pins)
suite 246_runner_offered_slots_suite.sql  # 0215 — 0203 shipped an `extra` (추가 근무) mechanism with a writer, a server honourer and NO READER: `is_slot_available` returns TRUE for a 추가 근무 window on a weekday with zero grid rows, and both owner-facing slot sheets build their candidates from `runner_availability_rules` ALONE (`runner-profile/[id].tsx:174`, `owner/reschedule.tsx:131`) — so `daySlots` is empty and `checkSlot` is never even called, while `runner/availability.tsx:494` promises the runner 「추가 근무는 그날 그 시간만 엽니다」. `runner_offered_slots(p_runner, p_from, p_to)` is that reader: the weekly grid expanded over a ≤90-day KST date range ∪ `extra` − `blackout` days, flat {day,start_min,end_min,source}, never the `note`. **0215-P1** an extra on a gridless weekday goes 0 rows → 1 row (delta) · **0215-P2** a blackout takes the grid's row AND the extra's away and gives both back on delete · **0215-P3** the offered set ≡ the `is_slot_available`-true set in BOTH directions over 14 days × 48 candidates on a mixed fixture, with three controls and the KST-midnight divergence family named and counted · **0215-P4** a confirmed booking reddens the JUDGE and leaves the LIST unchanged (§3–§5 stay with checkSlot, by design) · **0215-K1** a 23:59 UTC instant lands on the NEXT KST day · **0215-R1** refusal words + the 90/91-day boundary both ways · **0215-A1** a stranger gets the same rows an owner does (visibility is the feature) and the note never leaves · **0215-A2** deployed shape. — 0215-P1 ~ 0215-A2 (8 pins)
suite 245_ops_titles_audit_suite.sql  # 0214 — 0210 §B moved `kind='system'` out of the undisableable `safety` category on an enumeration of FOUR titles; the measured writer set is ELEVEN (12 sites, re-derived here from every `insert into notifications` whose kind column is `'system'` in the LATEST declaration of each function — 0118 writes it as a bare literal, which is why a `'system'::noti_kind` grep misses it — plus the five `kind: "system"` writers in `_shared/ops.ts`). Every one of the eleven is ADDRESSED TO THE OPS ROSTER, so the category is right for all of them and the enumeration was the defect; `0210-O2`'s four-element array could not see the other seven and would stay green as the set grew. 0214 §A lands `_noti_ops_titles()` (the eleven, by value) and §B makes the classifier's system arm TITLE-keyed: a ledgered title is `ops`, anything else is `booking` — still SENT by default, but gated by a switch its reader can see, because `notification-settings.tsx` draws 운영 알림 only behind `ops_me().is_ops` and a consumer muted by `ops` would be muted by a control they do not have. §C closes F5: `claim_gear_tx` fetched its row by id alone and raised `claim_not_found` before the owner was compared, so a stranger got two different words for a real claim and a random uuid; the locking select is now scoped to `auth.uid()` and both worlds raise `not_claim_owner`. — 0214-T1 ~ 0214-S1 (6 pins)
