suite 248_claim_deletion_lock_suite.sql  # 0217 — Codex 2026-09-25 #2 (READ, reproduced here MEASURED): `claim_gear_tx` (0214 §C) never read the caller's deletion state, and 0202 §B②'s redaction touches only rows that already hold `delivery` — so a `claimable` row survived deletion intact and a claim resuming behind the tombstone (a still-valid JWT, or a claim in flight while deletion commits) wrote a fresh name/phone/address that `ops_gear_claims_pending` listed and `ops_mark_gear_shipped` shipped, both gating only on the `{"redacted": true}` marker. 0217 §A locks the caller's `profiles` row FIRST, `for share` (the weakest lock that conflicts with deletion's `update profiles`; deletion's own order is profile row → claim rows, so the two cannot deadlock), refuses `deleted_at is not null` with ONE bare token `profile_deleted` before any read of `gear_claims` (a deleted profile is not a party; the answer is a function of the caller alone — own id, foreign id, missing uuid and NULL all get the same word — so no oracle; a caller with no profile row falls through to `not_claim_owner` as before). §B/§C join `profiles` and read the tombstone itself (pending excludes `deleted_at is not null`; ship folds it into 0202's `claim_redacted`, read in the SAME `for update of g` statement as status and marker — the join side unlocked so an operator's click never inverts deletion's order). Deletion is NOT patched again and no row marker is added (0217 §0d: a marker on an address-less row would say 「an address was removed」, the distinction 0202 §0b keeps; the row is inert by construction). **0217-D1** the live path is 0214's, bell included (claimed · five fields read back · bell == active payout_due roster · re-claim already_claimed=true rings nothing) — the positive control every refusal is measured against · **A1** 🔴 after the REAL deletion the leftover claimable row answers profile_deleted for its own id AND NULL, is byte-identical after, rang no bell, 0 addresses behind the tombstone · **B1** the hole's end state built by hand (claim live, then `deleted_at` stamped DIRECTLY so the redaction never ran — no marker, only the join can see it): its id and all five strings absent from the payload; controls: the live runner is listed with fields, a live profile's marker-redacted row still excluded · **C1** the same row answers claim_redacted to ship, writing nothing; 0202's order survives (tombstoned owner's shipped → already_shipped, claimable → not_claimed); control: the live claim ships with carrier + tracking · **E1** no oracle on either side of the tombstone — live stranger: foreign == missing == not_claim_owner; tombstoned stranger: foreign == missing == OWN id == profile_deleted; nothing moved · **S1** deployed shape, comments stripped: profile read + `for share` one statement and BEFORE the first `for update`; profile_deleted before ownership refusal and before the claim read; `v_deleted is not null` exact; 0214's scope kept, claim_not_found absent; both ops readers join profiles (pending `is null`; ship `(p.deleted_at is not null)` inside the `for update of g` statement, `v_tombstone is not false`); definer/search_path/ACL ×3; NO-FUNCTION/NO-SOURCE red — 0217-D1·A1·B1·C1·E1·S1 (6 pins)
